menu "RF certification test example"

config RF_CERT_EXAMPLE_INTEGRATED_OTA
	bool "Integrate coprocessor OTA (phy_cert_cp_ota)"
	default n
	help
	  Carries a coprocessor image in a LittleFS partition on the host and
	  streams it to the coprocessor over the hosted link.

	  Use it to put production firmware on a coprocessor whose own UART is
	  not reachable, once certification is done.

	  Off, none of it is built and the LittleFS dependency is not even
	  fetched; phy_cert_cp_ota still answers, with the steps to turn it on.

	  sdkconfig.defaults.ota sets this and the partition table it needs.

if RF_CERT_EXAMPLE_INTEGRATED_OTA

config RF_CERT_EXAMPLE_OTA_REPORT_VERSION
	bool "Report both firmware versions before sending"
	default y
	help
	  Reads the project name and version out of the staged image's app
	  descriptor and prints them next to what the coprocessor is running,
	  so an operator can see which image is about to replace which.

config RF_CERT_EXAMPLE_OTA_SKIP_IF_SAME
	bool "Skip the update when the staged image matches what is running"
	depends on RF_CERT_EXAMPLE_OTA_REPORT_VERSION
	default y
	help
	  Compares the staged image's version against the coprocessor's and
	  does nothing if they are equal, so repeating the command does not
	  reflash the same firmware.

	  Turn this off to send the image regardless — useful when the version
	  string does not change between builds.

endif

endmenu
